{"name":"Fitzgerald Smoke","hex":"#b3b6b0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"smoke","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The visible vapor/vapour, gases, and fine particles given off by burning or smoldering material.","A cigarette."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To inhale and exhale the smoke from a burning cigarette or cigar, burning material in a pipe, etc.","To inhale and exhale tobacco smoke."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smoke"}],"entries":[{"title":"Smoke","blocks":[{"text":"Smoke is an aerosol emitted when a material undergoes combustion or pyrolysis, together with the quantity of air that is entrained or otherwise mixed into the mass. It is commonly an unwanted by-product of fires, but may also be used for pest control (fumigation), communication, defensive and offensive capabilities in the military, cooking, or smoking. It is used in rituals where incense, sage, or resin is burned to produce a smell for spiritual or magical purposes. It can also be a flavoring agent and preservative."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Ognisko_ubt_0126.jpeg/330px-Ognisko_ubt_0126.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoke"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Smoke_chemical_composition.jpg/500px-Smoke_chemical_composition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Smoke_chemical_composition.jpg/500px-Smoke_chemical_composition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chemical composition distribution of volatile organic compounds released in smoke from a variety of solid fuels[4]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmoke_chemical_composition.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Diesel-smoke.jpg/330px-Diesel-smoke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Diesel-smoke.jpg/330px-Diesel-smoke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Emission of soot in the fumes of a large diesel truck, without particle filters","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiesel-smoke.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Wildfiretopanga.jpg/500px-Wildfiretopanga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Wildfiretopanga.jpg/1280px-Wildfiretopanga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Wildfiretopanga.jpg/500px-Wildfiretopanga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Smoke from a wildfire","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWildfiretopanga.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Muizenberg_Mountian_Fires_in_Cape_Town_of_2015.jpg/500px-Muizenberg_Mountian_Fires_in_Cape_Town_of_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Muizenberg_Mountian_Fires_in_Cape_Town_of_2015.jpg/1280px-Muizenberg_Mountian_Fires_in_Cape_Town_of_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Muizenberg_Mountian_Fires_in_Cape_Town_of_2015.jpg/500px-Muizenberg_Mountian_Fires_in_Cape_Town_of_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Smoke rising up from the smoldering remains of a recently extingished mountain fire in South Africa","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMuizenberg_Mountian_Fires_in_Cape_Town